[Choose your path]($link.page('start')) to get started.

# [Build with ZML]($heading.id('build-with-zml'))

Use the inference framework to implement, compile, and run models in Zig.
Follow the [ZML quickstart]($link.page('zml/quickstart')) to build MNIST with
Bazel and classify a handwritten digit on CPU. Check
[ZML hardware compatibility]($link.page('zml/reference/compatibility').unsafeRef('build-with-zml'))
for other build targets.

# [Serve models with LLMD]($heading.id('serve-models-with-llmd'))

Serve a checkpoint over HTTP. Follow the
[LLMD quickstart]($link.page('llmd/quickstart')) to start a server
and receive your first chat response. Check
[LLMD hardware compatibility]($link.page('llmd/reference/compatibility').unsafeRef('serve-models-with-llmd'))
for available runtimes. See [Operations]($link.page('operations'))
to deploy, monitor, and troubleshoot the service.
